1
00:00:03,161 --> 00:00:06,858
[Music][Drumbeats Continue]

2
00:00:12,270 --> 00:00:13,870
[Music]

3
00:00:23,481 --> 00:00:28,942
[Music] [Singing In Native Dialect]

4
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:33,616
[Music]

5
00:00:40,832 --> 00:00:42,432
[Music]

6
00:03:19,523 --> 00:03:23,721
Okay, swing.
That's it, swing.

7
00:03:23,794 --> 00:03:25,853
Nice and level.
Put it in there!

8
00:03:25,930 --> 00:03:30,060
[Native Dialect]

9
00:03:31,769 --> 00:03:35,398
Run! Run! Wrong way!
First! First!

10
00:03:35,473 --> 00:03:37,464
Wrong way!
Other way! Other way!

11
00:03:37,541 --> 00:03:40,510
Go, go, go, go!
Hold it! Hold it!

12
00:03:40,578 --> 00:03:44,708
[Man] Telephony!
Hey! Telephony! U.S.!

13
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:03,840
[Indistinct Chatter]

14
00:04:03,841 --> 00:04:06,561
These guys are great natural athletes.
Jerry, they're developing...

15
00:04:06,637 --> 00:04:09,071
their own unique style
of baseball here.

16
00:04:09,140 --> 00:04:12,109
I could file on African baseball
on a regular basis.

17
00:04:12,176 --> 00:04:15,339
- Maybe, you know, do a feature or...
- Yeah, that's fine.

18
00:04:15,413 --> 00:04:17,711
But enough of these
African baseball stories.

19
00:04:17,782 --> 00:04:20,046
George, there's an opening
on the sports desk.

20
00:04:20,117 --> 00:04:22,364
How soon can you and
Suzy get back here?

21
00:04:22,365 --> 00:04:24,611
Um, about a week.

22
00:04:24,689 --> 00:04:28,625
- When, when do you want me to start?
- Hey, man, we need you by Monday.

23
00:04:28,693 --> 00:04:33,289
- Do you want the job or not?
- Yeah! Uh...

24
00:04:33,364 --> 00:04:36,458
Get the cheeseburgers ready, Jerry,
because I'm gonna be home by Christmas.

25
00:04:36,534 --> 00:04:38,502
- Thanks a lot, buddy.
- See you soon.

26
00:04:38,569 --> 00:04:41,436
All right!
Ooow!

27
00:04:44,141 --> 00:04:46,701
[Whistle] Susan!

28
00:04:46,777 --> 00:04:49,837
I've got real news!
Wait till I tell you.

29
00:04:49,914 --> 00:04:52,041
I don't wanna miss Eric.

30
00:04:54,885 --> 00:04:58,343
Well, that's downright Jurassic.

31
00:04:58,422 --> 00:05:01,255
Fourth or fifth cervical
vertebra, don't you think?

32
00:05:01,325 --> 00:05:03,350
It's a neck structure
of a brontosaurus.

33
00:05:03,427 --> 00:05:07,761
- Small head, slender neural cord.
- Let's carbon-date it.

34
00:05:07,832 --> 00:05:10,892
- We could.
- I'll get it ready.

35
00:05:10,968 --> 00:05:13,960
Paris or London?
Shall I send a telex?

36
00:05:14,038 --> 00:05:17,030
- You could.
- What's wrong?

37
00:05:17,108 --> 00:05:20,009
This bone is about 80 years old.

38
00:05:21,312 --> 00:05:23,246
No.

39
00:05:24,615 --> 00:05:28,107
There's no point in showing
me that, Susan, my dear.

40
00:05:28,185 --> 00:05:31,916
I wrote it.
Don't you remember?

41
00:05:31,989 --> 00:05:34,321
This, I think, is more what
you should be looking at.

42
00:05:34,322 --> 00:05:36,653
Oh, no.

43
00:05:36,727 --> 00:05:38,957
It's not a giraffe.

44
00:05:41,298 --> 00:05:44,267
- Or am I just a total idiot?
- On the contrary.

45
00:05:44,335 --> 00:05:46,769
You're the brightest
post-doc we've had out here.

46
00:05:46,837 --> 00:05:49,135
Don't worry about it, my dear.

47
00:05:50,741 --> 00:05:53,574
- I thought I really had something.
- Excuse me.

48
00:05:53,574 --> 00:05:53,574
- I thought I really had something.
- Excuse me.

49
00:05:53,644 --> 00:05:55,839
- Susan, may I speak with you?
- Hello, George.

50
00:05:55,913 --> 00:06:00,782
I'm afraid that your wife has had a
slight scientific disappointment.

51
00:06:00,851 --> 00:06:03,012
- You all right?
- It's okay.

52
00:06:03,087 --> 00:06:07,046
I just wanted to find something
real important before I left.

53
00:06:07,124 --> 00:06:11,424
Susan, you know that most field
work is patience and frustration.

54
00:06:11,495 --> 00:06:13,929
You're young.
Don't rush it.

55
00:06:13,998 --> 00:06:18,935
In other words, some days you eat the
bone; other days, the bone eats you.

56
00:06:19,003 --> 00:06:21,972
Come on.

57
00:06:24,608 --> 00:06:26,838
Hi, Nigel. Ready to
sharpen his pencils today?

58
00:06:26,911 --> 00:06:30,813
- Must you always be sarcastic?
- Au revoir, Nigel.

59
00:06:32,716 --> 00:06:34,716
Is that Little Miss
Scientist's latest discovery?

60
00:06:34,716 --> 00:06:36,048
Yes.

61
00:06:36,119 --> 00:06:39,418
From Bateke. She's top-notch
at her job, Nigel...

62
00:06:39,489 --> 00:06:41,548
whether you like her or not.

63
00:06:41,624 --> 00:06:43,558
- Is it any good?
- I doubt it.

64
00:06:43,626 --> 00:06:48,063
Now don't patronize me, Eric,
please. I know that look.

65
00:06:48,131 --> 00:06:50,224
How good is it?

66
00:06:50,300 --> 00:06:53,235
[Eric] She knows nothing.

67
00:06:53,303 --> 00:06:58,172
If these scrapings are from Bateke,
I imagine the photo is true.

68
00:06:58,241 --> 00:07:03,008
- A trip is indicated.
- You do know that Etienne is dead.

69
00:07:03,079 --> 00:07:05,877
Oh, yes, terrible thing.
Fine scientist.

70
00:07:05,949 --> 00:07:08,168
Well, are you going to
tell her that we're

71
00:07:08,168 --> 00:07:10,385
going to Bateke because
of her scrapings?

72
00:07:10,452 --> 00:07:14,445
No, I'm not, and neither are you.

73
00:07:19,795 --> 00:07:23,287
Mmm, the beer that made
Ogbomosho famous.

74
00:07:23,365 --> 00:07:26,425
How about that? I can finally say
"Ogbomosho," and we're going home.

75
00:07:26,502 --> 00:07:28,404
The Post is really
lucky to get you. It's great.

76
00:07:28,404 --> 00:07:28,485
We'll miss you.

77
00:07:31,122 --> 00:07:33,522
- I'll write. I promise.
- Do that.

78
00:07:33,591 --> 00:07:35,525
- Good morning.
- Morning.

79
00:07:35,593 --> 00:07:37,633
I heard about your husband's job.
Congratulations.

80
00:07:37,633 --> 00:07:38,527
Absolutely splendid.

81
00:07:38,595 --> 00:07:40,728
It should suit him.

82
00:07:40,728 --> 00:07:42,860
As you know, I can
help you in Washington.

83
00:07:42,932 --> 00:07:45,560
You choose any school
or museum you like...

84
00:07:45,634 --> 00:07:47,864
and you'll get the highest
possible recommendation.

85
00:07:47,937 --> 00:07:49,962
Thank you.
I really appreciate it.

86
00:07:50,039 --> 00:07:54,499
One thing before you go. Dr. Pierre
Dubois from the Red Cross...

87
00:07:54,577 --> 00:07:56,511
is in the lab office.

88
00:07:56,579 --> 00:07:58,860
Could you have a chat
with him before you leave?

89
00:07:58,860 --> 00:08:00,141
Sure. Of course I will.

90
00:08:14,822 --> 00:08:18,883
[Chanting Continues]

91
00:08:26,550 --> 00:08:29,451
Where? Where upriver?

92
00:08:40,030 --> 00:08:42,362
George, thank you.

93
00:08:50,607 --> 00:08:54,338
You should bloody well tell me my
messages as they come in. - Okay.

94
00:08:54,411 --> 00:08:56,331
It is not okay. You make
things very difficult.

95
00:08:56,331 --> 00:08:58,073
Okay.

96
00:08:59,582 --> 00:09:01,846
Eric.

97
00:09:01,918 --> 00:09:04,546
Apparently your favorite
post-doc and her husband...

98
00:09:04,620 --> 00:09:09,387
are now chasing their bone
at a Sangha village upriver.

99
00:09:09,459 --> 00:09:12,951
- Where did you get that information?
- Dubois.

100
00:09:13,029 --> 00:09:16,055
- Red Cross.
- Damn it.

101
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:20,799
Blast it!
We're at the wrong place.

102
00:09:21,871 --> 00:09:24,601
Get me government house.
Tommy!

103
00:09:24,674 --> 00:09:27,700
- What is going on?
- You'll find out in due course.

104
00:09:27,777 --> 00:09:31,076
We're going to need
a boat and an escort. Tommy!

105
00:09:34,817 --> 00:09:37,479
She's a persistent
little devil, isn't she?

106
00:09:37,553 --> 00:09:41,546
If this is where they left the
carcass, then it should be here.

107
00:09:41,624 --> 00:09:43,717
Sounds logical.

108
00:09:43,793 --> 00:09:47,058
It must have washed with the current.

109
00:09:47,130 --> 00:09:51,066
We're gonna have to look over there.
What's downriver?

110
00:09:51,134 --> 00:09:54,570
Hey, Charlie.
[Speaking Native Dialect]

111
00:09:54,637 --> 00:09:57,105
[Native]

112
00:10:00,510 --> 00:10:03,206
No problem.
You won't get lost.

113
00:10:04,380 --> 00:10:07,543
This is the Kenge Obe
communications module.

114
00:10:07,617 --> 00:10:10,609
There's a transceiver.
There's a transmitter chip.

115
00:10:10,686 --> 00:10:13,086
You can... You can
beep each other.

116
00:10:13,156 --> 00:10:16,216
Also, the wraps and radio,
plus this excellent guide.

117
00:10:16,292 --> 00:10:20,888
Rent or buy? Food is extra. I'll be
back to pick you up in two days.

118
00:10:20,963 --> 00:10:25,127
Make it a rental and
tell him he goes with us.

119
00:10:25,201 --> 00:10:28,136
Hey, Charlie.
[Native]

120
00:10:28,204 --> 00:10:32,402
- [Native]
- [Protesting]

121
00:10:47,456 --> 00:10:50,619
No problem.

122
00:11:12,081 --> 00:11:14,675
[Susan]
Oh, my God! George.

123
00:11:14,750 --> 00:11:17,776
Hey! Where are ya going?

124
00:11:17,853 --> 00:11:20,913
[Native]

125
00:11:27,563 --> 00:11:31,260
"No problem."

126
00:11:54,423 --> 00:11:57,517
What a place, huh?

127
00:12:06,569 --> 00:12:11,029
Something big's been through here.
Look at those broken branches.

128
00:12:24,487 --> 00:12:29,049
- George?
- Come on.

129
00:12:30,993 --> 00:12:33,359
Oh, my God!

130
00:12:48,277 --> 00:12:53,078
[Native]

131
00:12:53,149 --> 00:12:56,778
- Hello?
- [Native]

132
00:12:56,852 --> 00:13:00,788
- [Native]
- [Native]

133
00:13:00,856 --> 00:13:03,222
Amigos.

134
00:13:05,928 --> 00:13:08,863
[Yelling, Laughing]

135
00:13:12,301 --> 00:13:16,863
George, maybe you should
give them something?

136
00:13:16,939 --> 00:13:19,737
- We would like to give you a gift.
- Huh?

137
00:13:19,809 --> 00:13:21,569
What would you like
me to give them, Susan?

138
00:13:21,569 --> 00:13:23,107
Show your watch.

139
00:13:23,178 --> 00:13:26,045
Show it.
Show them how it ticks.

140
00:13:26,114 --> 00:13:27,946
It doesn't tick. It's
a goddamn digital.

141
00:13:27,946 --> 00:13:29,776
Try it anyway, George.

142
00:13:33,220 --> 00:13:36,212
- You like my watch?
- [Beeping]

143
00:13:36,290 --> 00:13:39,088
[Beeping Continues]

144
00:13:39,159 --> 00:13:41,627
[Beeping]

145
00:13:41,695 --> 00:13:46,496
[Native]

146
00:13:46,567 --> 00:13:49,092
Have any other ideas?

147
00:13:49,169 --> 00:13:52,161
[George] Oh, terrific.

148
00:13:52,239 --> 00:13:56,403
It's a convention.

149
00:13:59,079 --> 00:14:03,038
Maybe they'd like my... pants.
It's what they could use.

150
00:14:09,356 --> 00:14:13,190
[George] Susan!

151
00:14:13,260 --> 00:14:17,094
- Susan! Don't! Their soul!
- It's okay.

152
00:14:18,565 --> 00:14:20,795
It's just a picture.

153
00:14:20,868 --> 00:14:25,601
It's okay.
Come on, it's all right.

154
00:14:41,388 --> 00:14:43,948
[Woman Laughing]

155
00:15:08,148 --> 00:15:11,879
Think happy thoughts.

156
00:15:13,887 --> 00:15:17,288
[Native]

157
00:15:23,397 --> 00:15:25,661
Mmm.

158
00:15:30,136 --> 00:15:33,105
[Laughing]

159
00:15:33,173 --> 00:15:37,166
[Laughing]

160
00:15:37,244 --> 00:15:40,111
I don't like it either, boss.

161
00:15:42,916 --> 00:15:45,783
- I'm George.
- Huh?

162
00:15:45,852 --> 00:15:46,646
- My name, George.
- Cephu.

163
00:15:46,694 --> 00:15:48,662
This I like.

164
00:15:48,730 --> 00:15:51,164
[Native]

165
00:15:51,232 --> 00:15:55,430
What is this stuff anyway?

166
00:15:55,503 --> 00:15:58,495
Near beer.

167
00:15:58,573 --> 00:16:01,474
It's near enough.

168
00:16:36,177 --> 00:16:38,372
[Susan] George?

169
00:16:38,446 --> 00:16:41,438
I feel really strange.

170
00:16:46,087 --> 00:16:48,851
Me too.

171
00:16:58,407 --> 00:17:00,967
Get down.

172
00:17:07,015 --> 00:17:10,849
The wind's at his back.
He can't get our scent.

173
00:17:13,622 --> 00:17:15,817
I need pictures.
Get my camera.

174
00:17:20,796 --> 00:17:23,959
Quick!

175
00:17:24,032 --> 00:17:25,966
Susan.

176
00:17:54,162 --> 00:17:59,930
[Camera Clicking]

177
00:18:00,002 --> 00:18:02,163
- George, look.
- I see.

178
00:18:02,237 --> 00:18:06,936
- It's the female.
- How do you know?

179
00:18:10,112 --> 00:18:12,342
George, it's a hatchling.

180
00:18:13,415 --> 00:18:15,542
It is.
It really is.

181
00:18:15,617 --> 00:18:18,279
Take pictures.
Take pictures.

182
00:18:23,492 --> 00:18:27,895
We're looking at
150 million years ago. My God.

183
00:18:30,999 --> 00:18:34,992
You realize you're gonna be the
most famous scientist in the world?

184
00:18:35,070 --> 00:18:37,163
And you're gonna cover it.

185
00:18:42,236 --> 00:18:46,696
What I don't understand is what
they're doing this far south.

186
00:18:46,773 --> 00:18:49,901
What I don't understand is
what they're doing alive.

187
00:18:49,977 --> 00:18:54,539
Ready? Maybe they ran out of this
fruit where they used to live.

188
00:18:54,615 --> 00:18:59,211
- Think that's enough?
- Yeah, okay.

189
00:18:59,286 --> 00:19:02,653
Following the food supply.
You know, George, that's not bad.

190
00:19:02,723 --> 00:19:06,181
- I guess we can get a little closer.
- You know what we've got to do?

191
00:19:06,260 --> 00:19:07,980
We've got to get them
used to us so we can

192
00:19:07,980 --> 00:19:09,660
stick one of Kenge's
radio chips on them.

193
00:19:09,660 --> 00:19:12,358
Jump back, Jack.

194
00:19:13,465 --> 00:19:15,399
Woo! Look at you! Aah!

195
00:19:17,002 --> 00:19:21,029
- George of the jungle.
- Come on.

196
00:19:21,106 --> 00:19:25,907
- [Growling]
- Chow time.

197
00:19:33,785 --> 00:19:37,516
They're getting used to us.

198
00:19:45,697 --> 00:19:49,133
Great. They love it.

199
00:19:51,770 --> 00:19:56,605
[George]
That's it, guys. Pig out.

200
00:20:10,956 --> 00:20:13,754
[Cooing]

201
00:20:13,825 --> 00:20:17,727
Hey, look. Behind you.
The baby. Terrific.

202
00:20:17,796 --> 00:20:20,697
You can put the transmitter on him.

203
00:20:23,301 --> 00:20:26,395
- Hey! Hey, you! Leave that alone.
- [Braying]

204
00:20:29,174 --> 00:20:31,506
Oh!

205
00:20:31,576 --> 00:20:34,238
Susan, he's got big teeth.

206
00:20:36,915 --> 00:20:39,440
Where'd he go?

207
00:20:42,921 --> 00:20:44,855
[Squawking]

208
00:20:47,892 --> 00:20:49,860
- You see him?
- He's underwater.

209
00:20:49,928 --> 00:20:52,988
On the right.

210
00:21:09,881 --> 00:21:12,816
George? George?

211
00:21:19,524 --> 00:21:22,459
[Screaming]

212
00:21:27,365 --> 00:21:29,663
Here, Baby, it's all right.
It's all right.

213
00:21:29,734 --> 00:21:32,464
God, George, you scared her.
No, no, no, stay here.

214
00:21:32,537 --> 00:21:36,871
- Real funny.
- Come on, it's okay. It's all right.

215
00:21:36,941 --> 00:21:39,933
Some food. Come on.
No, no, wait, wait.

216
00:21:40,011 --> 00:21:44,209
Here, here, here. No, no, come on.
Hungry? Free meal.

217
00:21:44,282 --> 00:21:47,183
That's it. Is it...

218
00:21:49,154 --> 00:21:52,612
Look at you.
Are you friendly?

219
00:21:52,691 --> 00:21:56,525
You like that? Yeah.

220
00:21:56,594 --> 00:21:58,926
Look at these ears.

221
00:22:01,900 --> 00:22:05,028
Wow.

222
00:22:05,103 --> 00:22:08,732
Yeah.

223
00:22:11,409 --> 00:22:16,779
Whoa, don't step on me.
Came to visit us.

224
00:22:16,848 --> 00:22:18,577
Yeah.

225
00:22:18,578 --> 00:22:20,306
She's like a little
elephant, isn't she?

226
00:22:24,022 --> 00:22:27,617
It's playing.
Dinosaurs don't play.

227
00:22:29,094 --> 00:22:31,528
- It's weird.
- Isn't her skin nice?

228
00:22:31,596 --> 00:22:34,531
I thought it would be more scaly.

229
00:22:34,599 --> 00:22:36,761
Well, you're not so bad.
You're kind of friendly.

230
00:22:36,761 --> 00:22:38,654
It's okay.
It's all right. Shh.

231
00:22:38,729 --> 00:22:44,190
[Chanting]

232
00:22:44,268 --> 00:22:47,999
[Growling In Time With The Chanting]

233
00:22:48,071 --> 00:22:52,701
- [Growling]
- Don't do that, idiot!

234
00:22:52,776 --> 00:22:55,540
[Eric] Oh, my God, she's had
more than 200 CCs already!

235
00:22:55,612 --> 00:22:57,603
Help me! Help me!

236
00:23:05,822 --> 00:23:09,553
Come on, you blockhead!
Take the rope!

237
00:23:11,762 --> 00:23:13,923
- She'll have to have a stimulant.
- I have it.

238
00:23:22,940 --> 00:23:27,775
Help me up.

239
00:23:27,844 --> 00:23:29,937
Right.

240
00:23:30,013 --> 00:23:32,208
Well done, Nigel.

241
00:23:32,282 --> 00:23:36,412
Really.

242
00:23:36,486 --> 00:23:38,602
You must excuse my
assistant, my dear Colonel.

243
00:23:38,602 --> 00:23:40,717
Heat of the moment.

244
00:23:42,458 --> 00:23:45,689
You know, I'm, I'm beginning
to take an active interest...

245
00:23:45,761 --> 00:23:49,162
in your career and, uh...

246
00:23:49,231 --> 00:23:51,791
you know I have
the aid of the president.

247
00:23:51,867 --> 00:23:57,464
One day I should like to
see you "General" Nsogbu.

248
00:23:57,540 --> 00:24:02,876
For all our sakes, we mustn't
lose this one, must we?

249
00:24:02,945 --> 00:24:06,005
Lose one, you keep one.

250
00:24:06,082 --> 00:24:09,245
I call that acceptable
losses, Professor.

251
00:24:10,236 --> 00:24:15,264
[Whimpering]

252
00:24:19,846 --> 00:24:24,613
[Moaning]

253
00:24:24,684 --> 00:24:29,451
[Growling]

254
00:24:32,993 --> 00:24:36,360
- [Whimpering]
- What's your problem?

255
00:24:36,429 --> 00:24:40,627
- Are you still hungry?
- [Groaning]

256
00:24:40,700 --> 00:24:43,260
She already ate 200 pounds
of of malumbo fruit.

257
00:24:43,336 --> 00:24:45,270
Oh.

258
00:24:45,338 --> 00:24:49,707
Who said you had to make
such a pig of yourself, hmm?

259
00:24:54,180 --> 00:24:56,546
You'll be okay.

260
00:24:56,616 --> 00:24:59,551
- Okay?
- [Groan]

261
00:25:09,496 --> 00:25:11,726
[Whining]

262
00:25:16,169 --> 00:25:18,103
[George] Oh...

263
00:25:18,171 --> 00:25:19,889
Get him outta here.
Ow! Get off my toe!

264
00:25:19,889 --> 00:25:21,606
She wants...

265
00:25:21,674 --> 00:25:26,475
- Oh, get off my foot!
- She's not feeling well.

266
00:25:26,545 --> 00:25:29,946
She's just a baby.
It'll be all right.

267
00:25:30,015 --> 00:25:33,644
- Oh, what breath!
- Shh.

268
00:25:36,955 --> 00:25:39,856
[George] Good God!

269
00:25:41,694 --> 00:25:45,460
- Come on, George. Come on!
- Heave, heave!

270
00:25:45,531 --> 00:25:49,451
[Groaning]

271
00:25:49,451 --> 00:25:52,849
Nifty. Ow!

272
00:25:52,921 --> 00:25:56,857
- Still hurts, huh?
- Look at the size of this sucker, huh?

273
00:26:03,932 --> 00:26:07,868
[George] Oh, yeah, that feels nice.

274
00:26:07,936 --> 00:26:11,770
- You like that, huh?
- Work your way up right there.

275
00:26:11,840 --> 00:26:15,776
Up, up, now to your left.
Right there.

276
00:26:25,720 --> 00:26:28,985
- [Cooing]
- Yuck!

277
00:26:29,057 --> 00:26:31,423
Come on, Baby.
Come on, come on.

278
00:26:31,493 --> 00:26:35,395
- Not now. Go on, go on.
- No, no, no.

279
00:26:35,463 --> 00:26:38,921
Get outta here.

280
00:26:45,840 --> 00:26:46,216
[Cooing]

281
00:26:59,287 --> 00:27:02,916
George, Baby...
Where's Baby?

282
00:27:02,991 --> 00:27:06,119
Baby!

283
00:27:06,194 --> 00:27:09,823
- Oh, God!
- I'm sure she's right around here.

284
00:27:09,898 --> 00:27:13,629
Baby!

285
00:27:13,702 --> 00:27:16,796
Baby!

286
00:27:16,872 --> 00:27:19,432
I don't know how she'll
feed herself, George.

287
00:27:19,508 --> 00:27:22,534
She can't reach the malumbo.

288
00:27:22,611 --> 00:27:25,341
We'll just have to keep looking.

289
00:27:44,533 --> 00:27:49,334
- [Beeping]
- Wait a minute.

290
00:27:49,404 --> 00:27:52,965
- I got something here.
- Baby?

291
00:27:53,041 --> 00:27:56,841
- [Beeping]
- Yeah, she's over that way.

292
00:27:56,912 --> 00:28:00,499
[Beeping]

293
00:28:02,084 --> 00:28:04,052
George.

294
00:28:13,562 --> 00:28:16,190
Oh, thank God.

295
00:28:18,066 --> 00:28:21,832
[Cooing]

296
00:28:21,904 --> 00:28:24,168
[Sighing]

297
00:28:24,239 --> 00:28:28,733
[Contented Growling]

298
00:28:30,646 --> 00:28:33,672
- [Grunting]
- Baby...

299
00:28:35,951 --> 00:28:38,146
you don't belong to me.

300
00:28:57,105 --> 00:29:00,336
Just another legend?

301
00:29:00,409 --> 00:29:04,937
If we let it be.
Come on.

302
00:29:15,324 --> 00:29:20,091
[Braying]
